---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Resources" description="Curated ADHD resources worth reading, listening to and following." current="resources">

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero">
  <p class="hero-label">Resources</p>
  <h1 class="hero-title">Things worth <em>reading,<br>listening to</em> and following</h1>
  <p class="hero-body">A curated mix of organisations, researchers, creators and communities who actually understand ADHD family life. Not a comprehensive list. A useful one.</p>
</section>

<!-- FILTER BAR -->
<div class="filter-bar">
  <button class="filter-btn active" data-filter="all">All <span style="opacity:0.5;font-size:11px;margin-left:2px" id="count-all"></span></button>
  <button class="filter-btn" data-filter="podcasts">
    <span class="filter-dot" style="background:var(--eucalyptus)"></span>
    Podcasts
  </button>
  <button class="filter-btn" data-filter="social">
    <span class="filter-dot" style="background:#C07848"></span>
    Social &amp; YouTube
  </button>
  <button class="filter-btn" data-filter="academic">
    <span class="filter-dot" style="background:var(--blue)"></span>
    Organisations
  </button>
  <button class="filter-btn" data-filter="books">
    <span class="filter-dot" style="background:var(--clay)"></span>
    Books
  </button>
  <button class="filter-btn" data-filter="community">
    <span class="filter-dot" style="background:var(--lavender)"></span>
    Communities
  </button>
</div>

<!-- COUNT -->
<div class="count-bar">
  <span class="count-text" id="count-label">Showing all resources</span>
</div>

<!-- GRID -->
<div class="resource-grid" id="grid">

  <!-- ══════════════ PODCASTS ══════════════ -->

  <div class="card" data-category="podcasts" data-country="AU">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-podcasts">Podcast</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇦🇺 AU</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD Mums</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Jane McFadden</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Raw, honest conversations about ADHD parenting from an Australian perspective. If you've ever felt like the worst parent in the world at 7pm on a Tuesday, start here. McFadden speaks from lived experience, not theory.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">mothers</span><span class="tag">australia</span><span class="tag">relatable</span></div>
      <a href="https://adhdmums.com.au" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="podcasts" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-podcasts">Podcast</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">Tilt Parenting</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Debbie Reber</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Expert interviews about raising neurodivergent kids. 400+ episodes, 10 million downloads, consistently high quality. Covers ADHD, 2e, autism and the messy overlaps. Better for deep dives than quick answers.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">neurodivergent</span><span class="tag">expert interviews</span><span class="tag">deep dive</span></div>
      <a href="https://tiltparenting.com" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="podcasts" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-podcasts">Podcast</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">Women and ADHD</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Katy Weber</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Interviews with women diagnosed with ADHD, many of them as adults. If your ADHD was missed until adulthood, or you only figured it out after your kid was diagnosed, this podcast gets that experience specifically.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">women</span><span class="tag">late diagnosis</span><span class="tag">identity</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.womenandadhd.com" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="podcasts" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-podcasts">Podcast</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">Hacking Your ADHD</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Will Curb</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Short, practical episodes, most under 15 minutes. Good for when you have a commute, not an afternoon. Focused on strategies, systems and making ADHD brains work a bit better in everyday life.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">practical</span><span class="tag">short</span><span class="tag">strategies</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.hackingyouradhd.com" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="podcasts" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-podcasts">Podcast</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD Experts Podcast</div>
      <div class="card-creator">ADDitude Magazine</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Recorded webinars with psychiatrists, psychologists and ADHD specialists. More clinical than most. The quality control is high and the guest list is genuinely impressive. Use the topic search rather than starting from the beginning.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">clinical</span><span class="tag">expert</span><span class="tag">research-backed</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.additudemag.com/adhd-expert-webinars-podcasts/" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="podcasts" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-podcasts">Podcast</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD reWired</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Eric Tivers</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">For adults with ADHD trying to make their own lives work. Not specifically about parenting, but useful if you want to understand your own ADHD-driven habits before you can help your kid with theirs.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">adult adhd</span><span class="tag">productivity</span><span class="tag">habits</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.adhdrewired.com" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══════════════ SOCIAL / YOUTUBE ══════════════ -->

  <div class="card" data-category="social" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-social">YouTube</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">How to ADHD</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Jessica McCabe</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">The clearest explanations of ADHD on the internet. Research-backed, accessible, not condescending. Good for understanding why your brain works the way it does, and for showing your partner, teacher or employer the thing you've been trying to explain for years.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">explainer</span><span class="tag">accessible</span><span class="tag">research-backed</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@HowtoADHD" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="social" data-country="UK">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-social">YouTube</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇬🇧 UK</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD Love</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Zoe &amp; Alex</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">A couple where both partners have ADHD. One of the very few channels that shows the relationship side honestly: the miscommunications, the forgotten things, the moments where two ADHD brains crash into each other. Funny and genuinely useful.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">couples</span><span class="tag">relationship</span><span class="tag">both ADHD</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@ADHDLove" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="social" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-social">YouTube</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">Dr. Russell Barkley</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Russell Barkley PhD</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Long, lecture-style videos from the most cited ADHD researcher alive. Not light viewing. But if you want to understand what ADHD actually is at a biological level, why it's not a motivation problem, and why willpower doesn't fix it, this is where the science lives.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">research</span><span class="tag">clinical science</span><span class="tag">deep dive</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@russellbarkleyphd2023" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="social" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-social">Instagram</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">Dani Donovan</div>
      <div class="card-creator">@danidonovan</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Infographics and illustrations that explain ADHD experiences in a way words often can't. The "ADHD paralysis" and "time blindness" posts are particularly good for showing people who don't have ADHD what it actually feels like inside.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">visual</span><span class="tag">infographic</span><span class="tag">shareable</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.danidonovan.com" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="social" data-country="International">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-social">Instagram</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🌐 International</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD Alien</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Pina Varnel · @adhd_alien</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Simple webcomics about what living with ADHD actually feels like from the inside. The kind of thing you screenshot and send to your partner with no caption because it says everything. Good for reducing shame. Yours and theirs.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">comics</span><span class="tag">relatable</span><span class="tag">shame reduction</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.instagram.com/adhd_alien/" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Follow <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="social" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-social">YouTube / Facebook</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free + Paid</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD Dude</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Ryan Wexelblatt</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Focused specifically on parents of boys with ADHD. Practical, direct and non-judgemental. The free content on YouTube is solid. The paid membership includes courses and live Q&amp;A sessions. Note: this is about parenting your child, not about your own ADHD.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">boys</span><span class="tag">parenting</span><span class="tag">practical</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.adhddude.com" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══════════════ ORGANISATIONS ══════════════ -->

  <div class="card" data-category="academic" data-country="AU">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-academic">Organisation</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇦🇺 AU</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD Australia</div>
      <div class="card-creator">National advocacy body</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Australia's national ADHD support and advocacy organisation. Good starting point for navigating Australian ADHD services, finding local support groups, understanding advocacy efforts and following what's happening at a policy level.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">australia</span><span class="tag">official</span><span class="tag">support</span></div>
      <a href="https://adhdaustralia.org.au" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="academic" data-country="AU">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-academic">Clinical guideline</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇦🇺 AU</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">Australian ADHD Clinical Practice Guideline</div>
      <div class="card-creator">AADPA</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">The evidence-based guidelines that Australian GPs, psychiatrists and psychologists should be following. Useful if you want to understand what good clinical care looks like, or if you feel like you're not getting it. The parent-facing summary is the most accessible entry point.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">australia</span><span class="tag">clinical</span><span class="tag">evidence-based</span></div>
      <a href="https://aadpa.com.au/clinical-practice-guideline/" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="academic" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-academic">Organisation</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇺🇸 US</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">CHADD</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Children and Adults with ADHD</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">The largest US ADHD advocacy organisation, with 200+ local chapters. Good research summaries, webinars and an ADHD professional directory. Reliable and well-maintained. The "About ADHD" section is a solid reference.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">us</span><span class="tag">advocacy</span><span class="tag">research</span></div>
      <a href="https://chadd.org" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="academic" data-country="UK">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-academic">Organisation</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇬🇧 UK</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADHD UK</div>
      <div class="card-creator">UK charity</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">UK-focused charity for adults with ADHD. Strong on explaining the NHS pathway, your rights under Right to Choose, and what to do when you've been waiting 3 years for an assessment. Very honest about how difficult the system is to navigate.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">uk</span><span class="tag">nhs</span><span class="tag">adult adhd</span></div>
      <a href="https://adhduk.co.uk" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="academic" data-country="CA">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-academic">Organisation</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🇨🇦 CA</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">CADDAC</div>
      <div class="card-creator">Centre for ADHD Awareness Canada</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Canada's primary ADHD advocacy organisation. Information on assessment, diagnosis and support across provinces. Note: pathways vary significantly by province, so use the provincial resources alongside national information.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">canada</span><span class="tag">advocacy</span><span class="tag">assessment</span></div>
      <a href="https://caddac.ca" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="academic" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-academic">Website</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🌐 International</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">ADDitude Magazine</div>
      <div class="card-creator">additudemag.com</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">The largest ADHD content resource online. Dense, sometimes overwhelming, but the research-backed articles are genuinely good. Use the search bar for specific topics rather than browsing. The expert webinar library alone is worth the visit.</p>
    <div class="card-footer">
      <div class="card-tags"><span class="tag">research</span><span class="tag">parenting</span><span class="tag">adult adhd</span></div>
      <a href="https://www.additudemag.com" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 6H9.5M9.5 6L6.5 3M9.5 6L6.5 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-category="academic" data-country="US">
    <div class="card-top">
      <div class="card-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-type-academic">Website</span>
        <span class="badge badge-country">🌐 International</span>
      </div>
      <span class="free-badge">Free</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card-title">Understood.org</div>
      <div class="card-creator">understood.org</div>
    </div>
    <p class="card-desc">Broad neurodivergence resource covering ADHD, dyslexia, autism and co-occurring conditions. Good for explaining ADHD to schools, understanding what's happening in your child's brain, and making sense of co-occurring conditions. More US-centric than it claims to be.</p>
